---
/**
 * HOW TO EMBED. The page a journalist, a law firm blogger or a newsletter
 * writer lands on when they want the map on their own site.
 *
 * THE CREDIT LINE IS THE POINT, AND IT SITS OUTSIDE THE FRAME. A link inside
 * an iframe belongs to the framed page, not to the page doing the framing, so
 * it earns the embedding site's readers a way to click through but it is not a
 * link FROM that site. The line of ordinary HTML under the iframe is. That is
 * why each snippet below is two elements and the terms ask for both.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { readFileSync, existsSync } from 'node:fs';

const laws = existsSync('content/laws/index.json') ? JSON.parse(readFileSync('content/laws/index.json', 'utf8')) : { total: 0, generated: '' };
const suits = existsSync('content/lawsuits/lawsuits.json') ? JSON.parse(readFileSync('content/lawsuits/lawsuits.json', 'utf8')) : { count: 0 };

const mapCode = `<iframe src="https://theworldofai.org/embed/ai-laws-map/" title="AI Laws by State, from The World of AI" width="100%" height="660" style="border:0;max-width:1100px" loading="lazy"></iframe>
<p>Source: <a href="https://theworldofai.org/ai-laws/">The World of AI, AI Laws by State</a></p>`;
const badgeCode = `<iframe src="https://theworldofai.org/embed/ai-lawsuit-count/" title="AI lawsuits tracked, from The World of AI" width="352" height="215" style="border:0" loading="lazy"></iframe>
<p>Source: <a href="https://theworldofai.org/ai-lawsuits/">The World of AI Lawsuit Tracker</a></p>`;
const desc = 'Free embeddable widgets from The World of AI: a live map of AI laws by state and a live count of AI lawsuits. Copy one snippet, keep the credit line.';
---
<Base title="Embed our data: a live AI laws map and lawsuit count — The World of AI" description={desc} current="/embed/">
  <h1>Embed our data</h1>
  <p class="answer">Two live widgets, free to use on any website: a map of AI laws by state covering
    <b>{Number(laws.total || 0).toLocaleString('en-US')} bills</b>, and a count of the
    <b>{Number(suits.count || 0).toLocaleString('en-US')} AI lawsuits</b> this site tracks. Each updates itself
    every day, so a number you publish today is still right next month. Copy a snippet below and keep the credit line.</p>

  <h2>AI laws by state, the map</h2>
  <p>A clickable map of every state. A reader who picks a state opens that state's AI laws page
    here in a new tab. Best at full column width. The map needs about 660 pixels of height on a desktop.</p>
  <div class="preview"><iframe src="/embed/ai-laws-map/" title="Preview of the AI laws map" width="100%" height="660" loading="lazy"></iframe></div>
  <p class="meta-line">Copy this:</p>
  <pre class="code"><code>{mapCode}</code></pre>

  <h2>AI lawsuits tracked, the count</h2>
  <p>A small card for a sidebar or the end of an article: the number of AI lawsuits in United States courts,
    the three most sued companies, and the date. It is 352 pixels wide and 215 tall.</p>
  <div class="preview small"><iframe src="/embed/ai-lawsuit-count/" title="Preview of the lawsuit count" width="352" height="215" loading="lazy"></iframe></div>
  <p class="meta-line">Copy this:</p>
  <pre class="code"><code>{badgeCode}</code></pre>

  <h2>Terms, in plain English</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Free for any site, commercial or not. No account, no key, no limit.</li>
    <li>Keep the credit line under the widget, with its link. That is the whole price.</li>
    <li>Do not alter the widget to remove the source or to suggest the data is yours.</li>
    <li>The figures come from LegiScan and CourtListener through this site's daily pipeline. If you
      quote a number in your own text, name the date beside it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Prefer the raw numbers?</h2>
  <p>The same data is published as open JSON for developers: <a href="/api/">the API index</a> lists
    every endpoint, including <a href="/api/laws.json">laws.json</a> and <a href="/api/lawsuits.json">lawsuits.json</a>.
    For a written summary to cite, see <a href="/state-of-ai-laws/">the State of AI Laws report</a>.</p>

  <p class="meta-line">Trouble embedding, or want a different size or a widget for something else we track?
    <a href="/contact/">Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>

<style>
  .preview { border: 1px solid #e8e2d4; border-radius: 12px; padding: 8px; background: #fff; margin: 12px 0 6px; }
  .preview.small { display: inline-block; background: #faf8f3; }
  .preview iframe { border: 0; display: block; max-width: 100%; }
  .code { background: #12102e; color: #f3f1ff; border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; overflow-x: auto;
    font: 13px/1.6 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
  .code code { background: none; color: inherit; padding: 0; }
</style>
